# v0.7.2 PATCH — release-CLI acs-verified gate parser-scoping fix

2026-05-10. Sealed local; awaiting dispatcher dogfood publish per
ASK-FIRST. v0.7.2 closes the cross-reference-AC-ID parser-scoping
defect surfaced at v0.7.1 publish-time and captured at
docs/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md line 232.

Defect-closure shape (no new outcome capability). The
`check_acs_verified` gate in framework/tools/loam/src/loam_cli/
release/gates.py previously scanned the entire plan-doc body for
AC.<scope>.<n> tokens and asserted each was GREEN-marked in
§status. The scan was too greedy: cross-reference AC IDs in §6
(out-of-scope explanations) and §8 (predecessor dependencies)
were treated as in-scope ACs requiring §status verdicts. v0.7.1
publish hit this twice (AC.NTU.6 in §6, AC.V060.7 in §8) and was
worked around by rewriting the cross-references as prose, losing
AC-ID precision.

AC.READYP.1 — Parser scope-restriction. check_acs_verified now
parses the plan-doc body for the `## §4 — Acceptance criteria`
heading, extracts the slice between that heading and the next
`## §<n>` boundary, then runs the AC-ID regex against that slice
only. Heading-recognition is permissive across the three observed
forms (em-dash, hyphen, no-separator). Absent §4 returns RED with
a corrective hint (no fall-back to whole-doc scan).

AC.READYP.2 — Restored AC-ID precision in v0.7.1 plan-doc. Two
cross-reference rewrites reverted to AC-ID form: §6 line restores
`AC.NTU.6 deeper F-DESIGN finding`; §8 line restores
`per AC.V060.7 dogfood`.

AC.READYP.3 — Test pair extended. New positive test asserts the
fixed parser ignores cross-reference AC IDs in §6/§8 when §4 ACs
are GREEN-marked in §status; new negative test asserts the parser
still RED-flags missing §4-declared ACs by name. Existing
test_AC_V060_2_* tests continue to pass.

AC.READYP.4 — Outcome-altitude probe. `loam release v0.7.2
--dry-run` runs against this very plan-doc and the acs-verified
gate returns GREEN naming the 5 in-scope ACs (AC.READYP.{1-4,S}).
Probe documented in docs/experiments/v0-7-2-hard-smoke.md.

